; bal -V --unrealized books no unrealized gain on a holding the report
; cannot value.  ACME is declared with N, so it has no market price and
; stays in its own commodity; only the AAPL lot is revalued, and the
; report total is what -V leaves unvalued (10 ACME against the $500 it
; cost).  Booking ACME at its cost instead would print an Equity:Unrealized
; Gains row of "$500 / -10 ACME", mixing the cost with the held commodity.
; Under --dc both holdings stay in the debit column, ACME in its own
; commodity, and the one unrealized row is the AAPL revaluation.

N ACME

2024/01/01 Buy ACME
    Assets:Private          10 ACME @ $50
    Assets:Checking

2024/01/01 Buy AAPL
    Assets:Brokerage        10 AAPL @ $150
    Assets:Checking

P 2024/03/01 AAPL $170
P 2024/03/01 ACME $75

test bal -V --unrealized
               $-300
             10 ACME  Assets
               $1700    Brokerage
              $-2000    Checking
             10 ACME    Private
               $-200  Equity:Unrealized Gains
--------------------
               $-500
             10 ACME
end test

test bal -V --unrealized --dc
         $1700
       10 ACME          $2000          $-300
                                 10 ACME  Assets
         $1700              0          $1700    Brokerage
             0          $2000         $-2000    Checking
       10 ACME              0        10 ACME    Private
          $200              0          $-200  Equity:Unrealized Gains
-------------- -------------- --------------
         $1500
       10 ACME          $2000          $-500
                                 10 ACME
end test
